{"kind":"artifact","text":"The architecture reference states the admitted-time authority rule and the layer 5 to layer 7 derivation boundary, and records this projection change as workroom-fold@14. Exact clean pushed head 97a749ecd8a27e57eb6c301f822f105bda391249 on request/planner-dr-recut; tree ad191b80cb5cd5edd11bd632f9dc029cc8e0968d, checkout clean, local and origin identical. Successor to c9d4f040 at this path.\n\nThe page is byte-identical to the withdrawn 05c39532 and to my parent e1798050. It is republished so every path's artifact stands at one exact head.\n\nTHE THREE PROFILE NUMBERS ON THIS PAGE ARE THREE DIFFERENT FACTS. Line 815 states that this projection change advances the profile to @14. Line 701 still states @13, which is main's guarded unclaimed-reassignment bump and is historically accurate. Line 796 still states @12 for the older change. Renumbering any of them to match the newest would make the page describe a history that did not happen. I checked this rather than assuming it, because the temptation on a recut is to tidy numbers into agreement.\n\nONE PASSAGE THIS LANE RELIES ON AND DID NOT WRITE. The page already states that a departed actor may still supersede an earlier act they authored, and that the narrow cleanup exception confers no force on a new state or a ratification. That sentence is load-bearing: it is why own-author withdraw stays outside the participant predicate while publish is inside it — now at three sites including the signing boundary. Claude once described that withdraw as a false offer, contradicting this page; codex caught it and the page was right.\n\nWHY THIS RESTS ON BEHAVIOUR ARTIFACTS AND NOT ONLY THE PROMISE. A documentation artifact resting only on its promise can never be flared by a change to what it describes. This one rests on the ui artifact at this head and on the live in-main predecessor at this path, so a later change to the behaviour it documents will reach it.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD: go test ./... -count=1 exit 0 with 34 ok and zero cached, which matters here because the docset gate caches past documentation edits; gofmt clean; build and vet exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"97a749ecd8a27e57eb6c301f822f105bda391249","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}